-- title:
--   Existence of a moduli place for every Γ₀(N)-moduli point
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N\ge 1$ an integer with $N\neq 0$ in $K$, and let $F_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $K$ the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d$ of $j$ for the nonzero divisors $d\mid N$. Let $x$ be a moduli point of level $N$ over $K$, i.e. a class in the quotient of the set of data $(E,g)$ with $E$ a Weierstrass curve over $K$ with invertible discriminant and $g$ a point of the affine model of exact additive order $N$, by the relation: a variable change $\gamma$ carries $E$ to $E'$ and $g'=k\cdot(\gamma^{-1}\text{-transport of }g)$ for some $k$ coprime to $N$. The assertion is that there is a place $v$ of $F_N$ over $K$ — a valuation subring containing $K$, proper, and a principal ideal ring — which is a moduli place of $x$: for some field $\Omega$ over $K$ there is a test datum consisting of a place $W$ of $\Omega$ over $K$, a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E$ over $\mathcal O_W$ whose reduction has nonzero discriminant, a point $g\in\mathcal E(\Omega)$ of exact order $N$, a $K$-retraction $\mathrm{res}$ of the residue field of $\mathcal O_W$ onto $K$ such that the reduction of $g$ has order $N$ and the reduced pair, transported by $\mathrm{res}$, represents $x$, together with a $K$-algebra embedding $\psi\colon F_N\to\Omega$ satisfying, in every algebraically closed extension $\Omega'$ of $\Omega$ and for every nonzero $d\mid N$, $\psi(\mathtt{jqNFull}\,K\,N\,d)=\mathcal E_{\Omega'}.\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}$ at level $d$ of the subgroup generated by $(N/d)\cdot g$; and finally $v$'s valuation subring is $\psi^{-1}(\mathcal O_W)$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the moduli description of the places of the modular function field of level $N$ over an algebraically closed field in which $N$ is invertible: every isomorphism class of a pair (elliptic curve, point of order $N$) is cut out by specialising the generic pair, so that a canonical moduli place may be attached to each moduli point. It is used in the orbit descriptions of places on modular curves, for instance in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd comparison of class sets with supersingular places and in the construction of Diamond's full-level data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isModuliPlaceOf_nonempty.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ModuliPlace

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve

universe u in

theorem ModularCurve.isModuliPlaceOf_nonempty
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] [DecidableEq K] (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (hN : (N : K) ≠ 0)
    (x : ModuliPoint N K) :
    ∃ v : Place K (modularFunctionFieldFullC K N), IsModuliPlaceOf K N x v := by sorry
